msgstr "Last used"

msgid "Manage trusted devices"
msgstr "Manage trusted devices"

msgid "No trusted devices."
msgstr "No trusted devices."

#, php-format
msgid "Only %d recovery codes left. Generate a new set so you are not locked out if you lose your phone."
msgstr "Only %d recovery codes left. Generate a new set so you are not locked out if you lose your phone."

msgid "Only the account holder can set this up — nobody else can see or change their secret."
msgstr "Only the account holder can set this up — nobody else can see or change their secret."

msgid "Print"
msgstr "Print"

msgid "QR code for setting up two-factor authentication"
msgstr "QR code for setting up two-factor authentication"

msgid "Revoke"
msgstr "Revoke"

msgid "Revoke all devices"
msgstr "Revoke all devices"

#, php-format
msgid "Server time is %s. If this is more than about half a minute away from real time, every code will be rejected — check that NTP is running."
msgstr "Server time is %s. If this is more than about half a minute away from real time, every code will be rejected — check that NTP is running."

msgid "Set up two-factor authentication"
msgstr "Set up two-factor authentication"

msgid "These browsers skip the code screen until their trust expires. Revoke any you no longer use or recognise."
msgstr "These browsers skip the code screen until their trust expires. Revoke any you no longer use or recognise."

msgid "These codes are shown once and cannot be retrieved again. Save them somewhere safe and away from the device running your authenticator app — they are the only way back in if you lose your phone."
msgstr "These codes are shown once and cannot be retrieved again. Save them somewhere safe and away from the device running your authenticator app — they are the only way back in if you lose your phone."

msgid "This removes the second factor from another person’s account. Only do this when you are certain who you are talking to — anyone who can pass this check can take the account over with the password alone."
msgstr "This removes the second factor from another person’s account. Only do this when you are certain who you are talking to — anyone who can pass this check can take the account over with the password alone."

msgid "This removes the second factor from your account, deletes your recovery codes, and signs out every device you had marked as trusted. Your account will be protected by its password alone."
msgstr "This removes the second factor from your account, deletes your recovery codes, and signs out every device you had marked as trusted. Your account will be protected by its password alone."

